WEBVTT

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.810
I've always been bad at playing.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.630
Come on, give me your hand!

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.490
W-Wait for me!

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.320
I couldn't really figure out
what I find to be "fun."

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.200
So maybe I was just waiting for this.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.670
Miki.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.210
Miki-chan!

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:38.630
Yes, waiting to meet someone
who can help me find what "fun" is.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:17.730
The usual morning, the usual classroom...

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.480
That place has the best pancakes...

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.590
What kind of school rule is that?!
Kyoto is over the top!

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.200
That's how it works here in
Kamogawa North High School!

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.780
This moment before homeroom is
the busiest, noisiest moment of the day.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:31.160
You're not allowed to enter cafés
and other entertainment establishments

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.290
on weekdays after 6 PM!
Don't forget, Takayashiki-san.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:39.550
What's taking the teacher so long?

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:40.970
Takekasa-san.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.170
Y-Yes, what is it, Class Rep?

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:49.010
We were planning to go karaoke this Sunday.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:53.430
A girls' get-together for the class.
You're coming, right?

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:56.230
Sorry... I have plans on Sunday.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.860
I'm uncomfortable with things
other people enjoy...

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:08.370
I can't get interested in things
that interest everyone...

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.740
I don't like places with lots of people.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.830
That's why I take the road
by the river when I go home.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:26.920
Taking a deep breath near Kamogawa River
helps me refresh the air in my body...

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:30.680
Out of the way, out of the way!

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.420
Oh, no... Can someone...

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.280
Hey, sorry about that! You okay?

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:53.420
I'm not the one who needs attention...

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:58.670
That was scary! The brakes just
suddenly stopped working!

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.380
I guess that's what I get for
getting the cheap rent-a-bike!

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.460
Thanks for watching out for me.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:05.010
D-Don't mention it!

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:09.550
Oh, wow, I'm soaked down to
my panties! Well, off they go then.

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:11.930
Please hurry, before someone shows up!

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.100
Oh, a Kyoto accent? Are you from around here?

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.260
I just moved here recently.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:23.060
You're always alone, so I figured
you're from a different area, too.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.550
Your name... Taka... Taka...

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:30.490
Takayashiki Aya from your class!
Nice to meet you!

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.300
I'm Takekasa Miki.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.620
P-Pleased to meet you, too...

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.090
You're lucky you had a
change of clothes with you.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:43.330
I just moved to the area, so I wanted to
do some Kyoto sightseeing after school.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:46.590
I'm glad I had extra clothes!

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.090
Though it's a bit breezy without panties!

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.300
Hey, do you have some spare time?

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.510
Huh? Oh, um, yes, but...

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.470
Cool! Can you show me around Kyoto?

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:58.840
I don't really get out of the house much...

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.520
I don't know the city at all...

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:01.890
Don't worry about that!

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.510
Okay! Let's go then!

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:19.500
Um... Go where...?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.170
Who cares? Just wherever our feet take us!

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:27.880
What?! We'd get lost if we did that!

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.590
Lost...

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:33.130
Yeah! Good one, Miki-chan!

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.010
Huh...?

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.510
Let's get lost today!

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:39.170
Get lost...?

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:50.590
Um, Takayashiki-san!

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:51.590
Yeah?

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:56.170
We've gone kind of deep
into the hills... Are we okay...?

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.800
Hey, Miki-chan, look at that!

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:01.130
What is this, a type of Jizo?

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.630
A duck!

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.380
Um, I mean, hey...

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.380
It has babies!

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.840
Baby ducks are so cute!

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.720
L-Listen to me!

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:16.170
Y-You've never been out here, right?

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:20.970
You don't know where we are,
you don't have a map...

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:26.340
If we walk around randomly like this,
we're really going to get lost...

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.840
There, there, don't cry.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.920
Miki-chan, I guess you lack skill.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.380
Skill...? What kind of skill?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.380
Playing.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.340
Huh?

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:48.670
Do you remember where we're headed?

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:51.550
Where? Nowhere...

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:55.170
Exactly! That, Miki-chan, is key!

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:58.470
In order to get lost,
one must first have a goal.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:06:59.720
Huh...?

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:01.720
Like, a shop you wanted to go to.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:07.010
Getting lost means there's some destination
we're failing to reach, right?

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:10.470
In that case, we can never get lost!

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:14.260
Because we don't have a destination!

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:18.300
I... I guess you're right...?

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.340
Yes, I just revealed a universal truth to you!

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:24.090
Thus, we are not lost. We're just pretend-lost!

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:25.590
Pretend-lost?

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:29.470
Yes! Pretend, therefore play.
Since we're just playing,

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:33.670
what you should be doing now
is not worrying about how to get home.

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:36.760
These unknown roads, views,

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:39.920
colors, sounds, smells...

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:43.050
Just enjoy them all!

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.510
Enjoy...

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:46.920
Come on, let's go.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:52.510
Okay.

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:08.590
Cool! What is this?!

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:11.050
I think it's an old water bridge.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.880
Wow, really?

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.130
Yes, I saw it in a textbook.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:19.510
Look, Takayashiki-san.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:30.220
So pretty... I didn't know
about this place at all.

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:33.550
I've lived in Kyoto all my life...

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:36.300
That's right, Miki-chan!

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.260
Huh?

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:42.130
The world has many more fun things
you don't know about!

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.720
It's what my dad always says.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:57.220
I thought there was nothing fun around me.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:04.470
But this made me think I could be wrong.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:08.920
Because, at that moment, I was smiling.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.630
See? Wasn't that fun, getting pretend-lost?

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:19.090
Yes.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:20.340
Let's do it again some time!

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:21.170
Oh...

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.220
Huh?

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:27.300
Isn't that our class rep?

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.260
Yeah, Ono-san...

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.970
We're in the amusement area, right...?

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.130
Yeah...

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:49.340
That walking rulebook class rep, here...?

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:54.760
You're not allowed to enter cafés
and other entertainment establishments

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:57.220
on weekdays after 6 PM! Don't forget!

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.550
It's already past six o'clock!

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:03.880
Let's find out where she's going! Hurry!

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:14.470
Such a random building in a back alley...

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:19.300
Let's go, Miki-chan!

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.920
Okay...

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.230
Saikoro Club...?

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.560
She's in here, right?

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:47.700
Wow, what is this?! So pretty!

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.840
I can't read this... What language is this?

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.130
It's German.

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:02.630
Hello, welcome to the Saikoro Club.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.220
Hey, wait, um...

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:10.760
Manager, I told you not to
talk to customers from behind!

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:14.670
You're face is too scary!

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:15.520
Huh?!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:16.690
Class Rep!

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:17.770
What...

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:19.400
You two...?

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:26.030
{Between}

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:30.320
Takekasa-san and Takayashiki-san...
What are you doing here?

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.630
Well, we saw you outside, and...

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.170
That's not fair, Class Rep!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:40.340
You told me not to break the rules,
but here you are at this hour!

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.630
All alone with this suspicious person!

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:43.470
What?!

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:46.550
I just work here!

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:52.130
As long as I have the proper permission
from school, I can work after six.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:55.390
You two need to leave, though!
It's against the rules to be here!

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:57.100
It doesn't make any sense!

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:59.560
How? I think the logic is perfect.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:04.880
Come on, relax, Midori-chan. It's not
like your friends visit you here often.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.700
They're just my classmates.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:12.920
Since you're here, why don't the
two of you stay and have some fun?

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.970
Fun? Fun how?

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:21.090
You're in a game store.
What else would we do for fun?

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:25.090
Games? Wait, are you saying...

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:27.800
...all of these are games?!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:30.800
Wait, you came in without knowing that?

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.760
This shop is dedicated to analog games.

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:36.920
These are all games...?

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:42.340
We focus mainly on European
board games, mostly from Germany.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:44.010
That sounds cool!

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:47.090
It totally is cool. Wanna try?

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:48.340
Yes! Let's try!

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:49.880
Right, then...

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.590
Hey, Manager!

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:54.760
Let's try this one. <i>Marrakech</i>.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:59.470
Hey, Class Rep, let's play!

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:01.380
This is one of your favorite games, isn't it?

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.590
No thank you.

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:06.840
Oh, well, the three of us can play then.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:07.840
Okay!

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:10.220
Thank you.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:15.260
One of the most important things when
playing a board game is imagination.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:17.840
Marrakech is the name of a city in Morocco.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:21.420
The board represents the market of Marrakech.

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:27.130
The goal of the game is to become
the best rug salesperson in this market.

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:29.470
Midori-chan, can you explain the rules?

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:31.840
Why me?

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:37.380
The player decides which way
the merchant, Mr. Assam, moves,

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.170
and rolls the die.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.800
By the way, this die only
has values from one to four.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.630
Two and three both have two faces each.

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:49.300
Mr. Assam moves the number of
spaces indicated by the die roll.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.970
Then, place a rug on a tile adjacent
to where Mr. Assam lands.

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:58.670
The rug can face in any direction,
but it can't completely cover another rug.

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:03.090
If Mr. Assam lands on another player's rug,

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:06.630
the player must pay one dirham
per square of connected tile.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:13.550
Repeat this process, and the player
with the most money at the end wins.

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:20.470
I see... So you put down lots of rugs and
get people to stop on them to make money.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:23.630
Yes, in a nutshell. Any questions?

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:24.970
Yes!

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:27.880
Why don't you speak in a Kyoto accent?

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.340
What kind of question is that?

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.420
Are you from the Kanto area?

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:34.630
No, I was born and raised in Kyoto.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:37.050
Then why?

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:39.840
The Kyoto dialect traditionally
includes many vague expressions.

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:42.260
It's not suited for logical thinking.

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:46.050
That's why I try to speak standard Japanese.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:47.090
Satisfied?

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:50.010
Oh, um... I see...

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:55.050
Okay! Let's get started then.
Choose a rug color that you like.

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:56.470
Yes.

00:14:56.470 --> 00:15:00.260
Now we rock-paper-scissors
to decide who goes first.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:06.510
Come on, one or four, one or four...

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:09.300
Please! Go!

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.300
No!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:18.170
You landed on my rug,
so you owe me three dirhams.

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:20.670
Why always me...

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:26.340
Manager, go easy on us please.
It's our first time.

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:29.770
Takayashiki-san, was it?

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:34.260
Every game I play, I play for real.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:39.550
Even if my opponent is a
child or a high school girl,

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:41.240
I don't hold back!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:47.620
Now, Takekasa-san, decide
which way Mr. Assam should go.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:53.340
What's wrong? Come on, hurry!

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:58.970
O-Ono-san?

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:04.970
Cut it out, Manager. It doesn't come off
as a joke when you say things like that.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:08.970
Go that way, it's safer. Roll now.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:10.190
Um, yes...

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:13.270
Midori-chan, that's against the rules.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:20.340
No chiming in on other people's games.
That's the rule here at Saikoro Club.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:25.670
You of all people wouldn't
break a rule, now would you?

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:28.340
You're right.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:29.470
Wait!

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:33.800
I really... I've never played
these types of games before.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.250
I don't know what to do.

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:40.840
So, um, um...

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:43.050
Takekasa-san...

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:47.470
Manager.

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:48.510
Hmm?

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:52.010
I think I'll join the game after all.

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.720
As her teammate!

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:59.470
I'm not chiming in on another person's game,

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:03.880
I'm just discussing strategy with a teammate.
That's not a problem, is it?

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:11.300
You're always so good at
finding loopholes, aren't you?

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.470
Thank you, Ono-san!

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:18.800
It's okay, I can't say no to
someone with that expression.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:23.050
But maybe it's too late...

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:25.130
Mr. Manager has too big of a lead.

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:29.670
Yes, it's a bit tough...

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:34.590
But the rug layout isn't too bad.
We still have a fighting chance.

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:36.420
Really...?

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:41.420
Yes, I will make you the number one
rug salesperson in Marrakech!

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:51.090
Hey, no fair! Help me, too, Class Rep!
I'm going to lose!

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:51.090
No, you're a rival merchant.
You're on your own.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:54.420
Come on! Class Rep!

00:17:55.470 --> 00:18:00.090
You need to be able to see how the future
plays out in order to win in this game.

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:04.590
How would your rug placement affect
the choices that other players make?

00:18:04.590 --> 00:18:08.420
What are the other players
trying to lure you towards?

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.970
Let's choose a different direction...

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:15.260
We should target bigger profits,
not avoid short-term expenditure.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:18.050
Our time to shine will come soon.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:20.510
Here, roll the die.

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:21.630
Yes...!

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:37.970
Now what do you want to do, Midori-chan?

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:40.220
Good move, Manager...

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:45.420
Ono-san, isn't that the manager's...

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:49.670
I know. But we have to take a risk here.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:52.470
But if we land on his rug, we'll have to pay...

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:58.050
...one, two, three, four,
five, six... seven dirhams!

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:03.130
Paying seven dirhams to the manager
now would be certain defeat.

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:07.670
But if we can roll a three or four here,
this risk can turn into an opportunity.

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:13.090
Turn a risk into an opportunity...?

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:17.420
If we keep running from the risk,
we just let the manager win.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.510
Now is the time to push forward.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.210
Push... forward.

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:27.340
Takekasa-san, I'm counting on your luck!

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.800
Y-Yes...

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:29.800
Here.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:35.010
Good luck, Miki-chan!

00:19:35.010 --> 00:19:37.760
Yes... Thank you.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:40.260
Here I come!

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:43.840
Three or four... Please... Three or four!

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.050
A four! Good job, Miki-chan!

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:51.340
Good job, Takekasa-san!

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:54.170
How's that, Manager?

00:19:56.380 --> 00:20:02.090
No matter which direction I go,
I have to roll a four or pay 11 dirhams...

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:04.050
Come on, Manager.

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:14.630
A two...!

00:20:14.630 --> 00:20:16.590
So...

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:17.720
Yes!

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.760
We beat him!

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:23.550
Wow! Awesome! Ono-san, did we just win?

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:26.420
That's right! All thanks to you, Takekasa-san!

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:29.260
No fair! I wanna join, too!

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:31.420
You're the enemy!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:33.340
Hey, come on!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:35.300
Don't be mean! Let's enjoy together!

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.660
I didn't know Midori-chan
had friends like this.

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:36.760
Stop clinging to me!

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:39.340
No I won't!

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:47.340
I had so much fun today!

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:51.170
I want to try playing those
types of games again...

00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:52.380
Yeah, for sure.

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:56.550
Hey, Class Rep! Can we visit you again?

00:20:56.550 --> 00:21:01.340
Today, I'm willing to overlook this
because the manager invited you.

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:02.170
Huh?

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:06.010
But if I catch you loitering
around at this hour again,

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:09.760
it is my duty as class rep to report it
to the school. You have been warned.

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.130
What?!

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:14.050
But if you want to play again...

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:18.920
Weekends and holidays
aren't part of that rule...

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:22.090
Ono-san...

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:25.220
I-I honestly don't care either way!

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:27.880
Just saying, if you want to play again...

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:29.220
Yes! Let's play again!

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.720
Hey, stop clinging!

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.470
Come on, why not?

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.340
Because I said so!

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:39.220
By the way, I noticed, your Kyoto accent
comes out when you're excited.

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:40.380
No it doesn't!

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.470
What? But it did back then!

00:21:42.470 --> 00:21:44.880
I said it doesn't!

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:49.970
She's right. The world might
have a lot of fun things

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.610
I don't know about.

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:57.380
Miki-chan, hurry!

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:04.370
That day, I found someone
who can look for "fun" with me.

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:42.640
We've decided to play a game with
Tanoue-kun, a boy Ono-san grew up with.

00:23:43.010 --> 00:23:46.430
Do I see something odd, though...?
Could it be...?
